OL,3,GNEWSAI was told I was too young to have
OL,4,Acancer - it had spread by the time I
OL,5,Awas diagnosed
OL,6,
OL,7,FA woman who said she was told by a GP
OL,8,Fshe may be experiencing "medical
OL,9,Fanxiety" after finding a lump in her
OL,10,Fbreast was later diagnosed with cancer.
OL,12,FBeth Jenkins, 42, visited a locum GP at
OL,13,Fher practice with concerns that a lump
OL,14,Fon her right breast had grown
OL,15,Fsignificantly. But she said she was
OL,16,Ftold she was "too young to have breast
OL,17,Fcancer" and it may be linked to
OL,18,Fpostnatal depression instead.
OL,20,FHowever, it was lobular breast cancer,
OL,21,Fwith a 5cm (2in) tumour and the disease
OL,22,Fhad spread to three lymph nodes.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
